# Build output
dist/
build/
*.exe
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.dll

# ...but ui/build is CONFIGURATION, not output: it holds the NSIS include and the
# certificate consent page the installer is built from. The bare `build/` rule
# above matches at any depth and would have excluded both, leaving a repo whose
# installer nobody can rebuild. Git will not descend into an ignored directory,
# so the directory itself has to be un-ignored before anything inside it can be.
!ui/build/
# The staged core + certificate are copied in by tools/prepare-core.js at build
# time and must NOT be committed (also caught by *.exe above; explicit is better).
ui/build/core/

# Logs / local runtime files
*.log

# Python bytecode. src/ ships the four validation analysis scripts, so anyone who
# runs one leaves a __pycache__ next to the sources; without this it shows up as
# untracked and can be swept into a commit by a careless `git add -A`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
